  "prompt": "CFF2 TTFont imported from TTX does not render glyph variations via getGlyphSet()\n\n```python\nimport io\nfrom fontTools.ttLib import TTFont\nfrom fontTools.pens.boundsPen import BoundsPen\n\n\nfontFromOTF = TTFont(\"cff2-ttx-test.otf\")\n\nf = io.BytesIO()\nfontFromOTF.saveXML(f)\nf.seek(0)\n\nfontFromTTX = TTFont()\nfontFromTTX.importXML(f)\n\nfor ttx in [False, True]:\n    font = fontFromTTX if ttx else fontFromOTF\n    print(\"from TTX:\" if ttx else \"from OTF:\")\n    for location in [{}, {\"wght\": 1000}]:\n        gs = font.getGlyphSet(location=location)\n        pen = BoundsPen(None)\n        gs[\"period\"].draw(pen)\n        print(pen.bounds, location)\n```\n\nOutput:\n```\nfrom OTF:\n(60, 0, 110, 120) {}\n(30.0, 0, 220.0, 300.0) {'wght': 1000}\nfrom TTX:\n(60, 0, 110, 120) {}\n(60, 0, 110, 120) {'wght': 1000}\n```\n\nThe last box is wrong, and should also be `(30.0, 0, 220.0, 300.0)`.\n\nI did notice that `CharStrings.varStore` is None when imported from XML, so that may be a clue.\n\n[cff2-ttx-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/34284421/cff2-ttx-test.zip)",
